🎯 What: Direct use of user input in regex search queries can lead to NoSQL Injection or ReDoS attacks.
⚠️ Risk: A malicious user could craft a search string that causes the regex engine to take exponential time to match, leading to denial of service, or execute unauthorized operations.
🛡️ Solution: Extracted the sanitization logic to a shared `securityUtils.js` file and applied it to all occurrences in `admin.js`, `productController.js`, and `storeController.js`.
